** Playbooks **

Teams use playbooks, sometimes called workflows, to respond to alerts or incidents the same way every time.

Playbooks work in unison with security teams by taking the steps an analyst would typically implement when responding to an incident.

+ Does repetitive tasks, such as compiling data into a report or sending emails.
+ Pauses when human oversight is needed (for example, implementing a firewall block).
+ Improves response speed and consistency while maintaining human authority.

Phishing investigations are one of the most common use cases for SOAR implemented by customers.

Without SOAR, an analyst will spend time investigating the sender of a phishing email and key indicators located within the email headers or body.

With a phishing investigation playbook, the initial investigation steps are taken automatically, as soon as the phishing email is reported.

This way, the analysts will be alerted to only those emails that the playbook determines are suspicious.
After the analyst confirms that a reported email warrants firther action, the playbook can continue making additional SIM queries, deleting the email
from all user inboxes, sending an email to all recipients alerting them of the action taken, and providing helpful tips on what to do if they
receive similar phishing messages in the future.

